>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SIntro`

``` hol4
clasetLib.SIntro : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a safe introduction rule for one tactic invocation.

`SIntro th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a marker recognized
in the theorem-list argument of the classical tactics. The tactic adds `th`
to its temporary classical rule set as a safe introduction rule. Such a
rule matches its conclusion against the goal and replaces the goal by the
rule's premises.

The modification lasts only for that tactic call. To register a stored
safe introduction rule persistently, attach the argument-free `[sintro]`
attribute to its theorem declaration. The plain `[intro]` attribute and
`Intro` marker instead classify an introduction rule as unsafe.

### Failure

Constructing `SIntro th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` cannot be converted to introduction-rule form.

### Example

This invocation makes `my_intro_rule` safe without changing the global rule
set:

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [clasetLib.SIntro my_intro_rule]
```

